/*Q10.
Chloe is developing a memory-efficient algorithm for a resource-constrained environment. She needs to swap values of two variables without using additional memory. Write a program that uses Bitwise XOR to swap two numbers, aiding Chloe in conserving valuable memory.

Input Format:
  - The two lines of the input are the integers that need to be swapped.

Output Format:
  - Print the swapped values in the following format:

    Num1: <swapped value of num1>, Num2: <swapped value of num2>

Note: A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: Three XORs swap the values without a temporary variable.*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int num1 = sc.nextInt();
        int num2 = sc.nextInt();

        num1 = num1 ^ num2;
        num2 = num1 ^ num2;   // (a^b)^b = a
        num1 = num1 ^ num2;   // (a^b)^a = b

        System.out.println("Num1: " + num1 + ", Num2: " + num2);
        sc.close();
    }
}
